{"overview":"Two wagon caravans converge at what is now Kansas City, and combine for the westward push to Oregon. On their quest the pilgrims will experience desert heat, mountain snow, hunger, and Indian attack. To complicate matters further, a love triangle develops, as pretty Molly must chose between Sam, a brute, and Will, the dashing captain of the other caravan. Can Will overcome the skeleton in his closet and win Molly's heart?","tagline":"The Cowards never started and the Weak died on the way.","cast":[{"n":"Lois Wilson","c":"Molly Wingate","p":"/fSQS8avO1WLCdD8BfDuwEtLLsCa.jpg","q":"Q275728"},{"n":"Alan Hale","c":"Sam Woodhull","p":"/e90MwAMkxjDqr3wOnOhDAjvylW5.jpg","q":"Q1971717"},{"n":"Ernest Torrence","c":"Jackson","p":"/g1Fhsm1aVrhK4lAW8GUz9w9SzZz.jpg","q":"Q281962"},{"n":"Tully Marshall","c":"Jim Bridges","p":"/4bBj7eZ2A8LjO1HZnHipjPhLu5Z.jpg","q":"Q2063267"},{"n":"Charles Ogle","c":"Mr. Wingate","p":"/hmSOnMuub9xJ606MsSZEqJg4fXG.jpg","q":null},{"n":"J. Warren Kerrigan","c":"Will Banion","p":"/bWB1MiTsBTtgOB1k89Nc5WJgfbF.jpg","q":"Q3072218"},{"n":"Ethel Wales","c":"Mrs. Wingate","p":"/8TspAWWfu1IvRbQ46FrD9hJrtoO.jpg","q":"Q3059263"},{"n":"Guy Oliver","c":"Kit Carson","p":"/tLe4A808lGBfSenS42k1ZeAdZEO.jpg","q":"Q3122043"},{"n":"Johnny Fox","c":"Jed Wingate","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Frank Albertson","c":"Bit (uncredited)","p":"/sT9JZ8GgHgunZS4PWIDX6wMoIS7.jpg","q":"Q3082484"}],"country":["United States"],"language":["English"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Covered_Wagon","qid":"Q587925","rel":{"US":{"d":"1923-03-15","c":"NR"}},"backdrops":["/jPYxPIumFONbym5ACyYedITYo3m.jpg","/eNdndCgRCl3ctsT33TawrSyKLDH.jpg","/v4Obzq0bQC4enZ287O78OsxAj6z.jpg","/ujs73Dtpk1O6Vb8AlgXrCTZjSol.jpg","/7T0hK2SLruziZOpGANI2cK2P9Kt.jpg","/eorpyipS1N6cyY6QEBH1bzTHsKT.jpg","/jTNEtdj3sY7urDwhKe4UvDA55Qc.jpg","/os2Bftx17E8O35hJZ1Det6ydWub.jpg"]}